\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{The remaining reconstruction question}
\date{2026-11-17}

\p{The finite reflection criterion in \ref{fdip-00XH} applies
to a declared algebra, functional and half. The cellular
cochain choices give the exact negative even element in
\ref{fdip-00XY}, alongside the separately positive
connection marginal in \ref{fdip-00XZ}. They do not
supply a fermionic Hilbert space or transfer evolution.}

\p{A different reflection or transfer construction must
identify its multiplication, adjoint, boundaries, gauge
constraint and observable map before a source positivity
theorem can apply. The fermionic transfer question in \ref{fdip-00JB}
therefore remains open beyond the stated cellular result;
a two-time-slice transfer operator, if constructed with
other reflection data, would require its own test.}
